<title>SPAIN: Mannesmann interested in Retevision's bid.</title>
<headline>Mannesmann interested in Retevision's bid.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Retevision said on Monday that Germany's Mannesmann AG was also interested in bidding for Retevision.</p>
<p>&quot;Besides the two groups led by BCH and by Endesa, Mannesmann also showed its interest in the auction for Retevision,&quot; a spokeswoman of Retevision said Reuters.</p>
<p>She did not add any details.</p>
<p>Earlier today, two groups said they would bid for Retevision, which would compete with newly privatised Telefonica de Espana.</p>
<p>One consortium, led by Spain's BCH (Banco Central Hispanoamericano SA), groups France Telecom, Deutsche Telekom and U.S. Sprint.</p>
<p>The competitor is made up of the Italian public holding STET, Spanish electricity group Endesa and Union Fenosa, and with the Basque group Euskatel.</p>
<p>Monday was the deadline for expressing interest in bidding. Bids are due by June 9.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
